-- #1111 A-2.5b — the promotion-bearing cell.  Its only difference from the sibling
-- `method_scope_valid_under_bystander` is the UNSIGNATURED CONSTRAINED FUNCTION
-- `twice`, which is what routes `elaborateModules` down its SECOND sweep (the one
-- whose first statement is another `resetCrossModuleState ()`).  It DOES reach that
-- path — at the pre-fix commit the emitted `twice` takes a dict param, so the
-- promotion arm demonstrably ran — but reaching a path is not observing its
-- consequence.  See the non-discriminating note below before citing this cell.
--
-- WHY `twice` CHANGES THE PATH.  With no direct promotion anywhere,
-- `promotionHarvestRef` is empty and #194's single bare sweep IS the final answer.
-- An unsignatured constrained binding is directly promoted, so the harvest is
-- non-empty, `elaborateModules` DISCARDS the bare sweep and re-runs — and the arm
-- it re-runs through opens with a second `resetCrossModuleState ()`.  Every one of
-- this unit's other five fixtures is promotion-free and takes the fast path, so all
-- five were green while `run` and `build` were broken.
--
-- EXPECTED VALUE DERIVED BY HAND: `msmth` reaches this module only through `msmid`,
-- which re-exports `msifb`'s, so both the direct occurrence and the one inside
-- `twice` mean `MSIB.msmth`; this module implements exactly that interface.
-- `twice Blob` is `"B" ++ "B"` = `BB`.
--
-- 🚨 NON-DISCRIMINATING IN THIS CORPUS — DO NOT CITE IT AS COVERAGE FOR F1.
-- This cell was added to catch F1 and it CANNOT: measured, it is GREEN on the pre-fix
-- commit 0772effb, and the emitted IR is byte-identical across the fix
-- (md5 2be2f2f1c32f95cec2b70f1680beb832 at both commits).  Two structural reasons, both
-- of which apply to `test/llvm_fixtures_modules/` generally:
--   1. this corpus's probe does not gate on type errors — `entry_support.runEmitWith`
--      (`compiler/entries/entry_support.mdk`) calls `elaborateModules` and emits
--      unconditionally, with no `hadTypeErrors` check.  F1's symptom is an obligation
--      recorded against the wrong interface, i.e. a TYPE ERROR, which this harness never
--      observes;
--   2. impl mangling here omits the interface — the IR carries `@mdk_impl_Blob_msmth` —
--      so with one impl of `msmth` for `Blob`, MSIA-vs-MSIB cannot move the symbol.
-- The same argument makes the sibling `method_scope_valid_under_bystander` and every
-- other cell of this corpus non-discriminating for F1, and `diff_compiler_engines.sh`
-- reads the same corpus, so it does not help either.
--
-- ✅ THE DISCRIMINATING CELL IS
--    `test/run_check_agreement_fixtures/accept_a25b_method_scope_promoted.mdk`,
-- which grades check/run/build EXIT-CODE AGREEMENT with the real prelude and a `.out`
-- value pin — F1's actual shape (`check` 0 while `run`/`build` 1).  Measured there:
-- FAIL at `$BASE`, FAIL at the pre-F1-fix tip 0772effb, PASS here.
--
-- This cell is KEPT because it still pins the accept-under-collision VALUE on all three
-- engines for a promotion-bearing graph, which is worth having — just not as F1 coverage.
import msmid.{MSIB, msmth}
import msifa.{MSIA}

data Blob = Blob

impl MSIB Blob where
  msmth _ = "B"

-- NO SIGNATURE, and constrained: this is the whole point of the fixture.
twice x = msmth x ++ msmth x

main : <IO> Unit
main = putStrLn (twice Blob)
